          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "Here are some good case / rack / chassis options & suggestions I found on **eBay UK** + from retailers, plus what to watch out for. These are \u201cgood enough\u201d for your server build, and mostly budget-friendly.  \n\n---\n\n## \ud83d\udd0d eBay UK / Used / New Listings\n\nHere are some relevant eBay UK / UK-based used or new-ish listings I found:\n\n| # | Item | Condition / Price | Pros & Potential Issues |\n|---|------|--------------------|--------------------------|\n| 1 | Fractal Design Define R5 Mid Tower PC Case - Used | ~ **\u00a3105 + ~\u00a37 postage** \ue200cite\ue202turn0search5\ue201 | Good tower case, very quiet, supports 6-8 drives (internal cages). Pros: very clean, good cooling, low noise. Con: Not rackmount; depth & footprint might be large. |\n| 2 | 4U Rack Mount ATX Server Case - \u201c4U500V2\u201d Brand New | ~ **\u00a3165** new from UK seller (PCArena\u2010Bristol) \ue200cite\ue202turn0search2\ue201 | Proper rackmount case, supports ATX/mATX, likely good for 6+ drives. Higher cost. Might carry more weight / depth. |\n| 3 | Heavy Duty 4U Rackmount PC Chassis, ATX/mATX/ITX | Listing (no price shown) in \u201c4U Rackmount Cases and Chassis\u201d section \ue200cite\ue202turn0search4\ue201 | Good generic option; check depth, drive mounting, how many drive cages included. |\n| 4 | Fractal Design Define R5 ATX PC Case \u2013 Good Condition | ~ **\u00a360** used (free delivery) or similar listings \ue200cite\ue202turn0search1\ue202turn0search7\ue201 | Excellent value for quiet tower; good number of 3.5\u201d bays; likely low noise. |\n| 5 | Generic new \u201c4U Rack-mount Case, 4U Server Chassis Supports 8\u00d73.5\u201d HDD\u201d | ~ **\u00a3170+** in \u201cserver case products\u201d section \ue200cite\ue202turn0search10\ue202turn0search2\ue201 | Supports many drives, specifically built for server use. Higher cost; check fan / PSU space. |\n\n---\n\n## \u2699\ufe0f Retail / New Case Options (Outside eBay)\n\nThese are new but give you a sense of what price/performance looks like for small rack or ATX-/mATX-friendly cases.\n\n\ue200products\ue202{\"selections\":[[\"turn0product1\",\"Codegen 4U-500 Rackmount Case\"],[\"turn0product2\",\"Codegen 4U Rackmount Case (standard)\"],[\"turn0product3\",\"Inter-Tech 4U-4098-S Rack Case\"],[\"turn0product4\",\"NICCOO 4U Server Case\"],[\"turn0product6\",\"Codegen 4U V2 Rackmount Case\"],[\"turn0product19\",\"Logic Case LC-4650-WH 10 bay 4U Chassis\"],[\"turn0product24\",\"OcUK Professional 4U Standard 10-HDD Chassis\"],[\"turn0product18\",\"Silverstone SST-RM400 Rackmount Case\"]],\"tags\":[\"good depth\",\"balanced price\",\"budget 4U\",\"value\",\"mid-price\",\"lots of drive bays\",\"pro standard\",\"premium\"]}\ue201\n\nHere are some highlights:\n\n- **\ue200product_entity\ue202[\"turn0product1\",\"Codegen 4U-500 Rackmount Case\"]\ue201**: 4U, reasonable depth (~500mm), good build quality.  \n- **\ue200product_entity\ue202[\"turn0product4\",\"NICCOO 4U Server Case\"]\ue201**: cheaper 4U; good if you only have a few HDDs to begin with.  \n- **\ue200product_entity\ue202[\"turn0product24\",\"OcUK Professional 4U Standard 10-HDD Chassis\"]\ue201**: supports 10 \u00d7 3.5\u2033 drives, nice option if aiming for bigger ZFS pool early.\n\n---\n\n## \ud83d\udee0 What to Check / What Matters\n\nWhen deciding between these cases, ensure the following:\n\n1. **Depth**: Rackmount cases vary in how \"deep\" they are. Measure your rack / space. If too deep, it may require rear support or may poke out.  \n2. **Drive cages / trays**: Make sure there are enough of 3.5\u2033 drive bays for your spinning discs, plus space to mount SSDs or cages. Also check how easy it is to mount/remove drives (access, screws vs tool-less).  \n3. **Fan mounts / airflow**: 1 or 2 large fans (120/140 mm) are better than multiple small ones; front filters help keep dust manageable.  \n4. **PSU placement and compatibility**: Your existing Seasonic GC500 is standard ATX, ensure the case supports ATX PSU positionally. Check cable routing space.  \n5. **Vibration / insulation**: Spinning drives vibrate. Good cases have rubber grommets, solid mounting; avoid thin metal rattling.  \n6. **Noise**: In a rack environment, doors or panel dampening affect noise. If it's going in a study, a quiet tower may still be preferable.  \n\n---\n\n## \u2714 Suggested Choices\n\nGiven your budget & priorities (quiet, cheap, learning, space for drives), here are my suggestions:\n\n- **Best \u201cbang for buck used tower\u201d**: Fractal Define R5 used (~\u00a3100) \u2014 good quietness, enough space for drives, low risk.  \n- **Best rackmount cheap new**: Codegen 4U-500 or Generic 4U rackmount ATX case if you find one sub-\u00a3120.  \n- **Intermediate \u201cstep-up\u201d**: OcUK 10-bay 4U chassis or any 4U supporting 8-10 drives, for future expansion.  \n\n---\n\nIf you like, I can pull together a shortlist of **4 rackmount cases under ~\u00a3120** on eBay UK (with pictures & exact dimensions) so you can directly compare. Do you want that?"
