              "Excellent progress \u2014 you\u2019ve done the hard parts: network driver, DHCP, and DNS.  \nNow we just need to restore **bidirectional reachability** and ensure the IP persists across reboots.\n\nLet\u2019s do this in three short steps:  \n\n---\n\n## \ud83e\udde9 Step 1 \u2013 Confirm the basics\n\nOn the Ubuntu box (rtr02):\n\n```bash\nip addr show enp3s0\nip route\nsudo ufw status\nsudo ss -tulpn | grep ssh\n```\n\n\u2705 You should see:\n- `enp3s0` has `inet 10.0.0.110/24`\n- Default route via `10.0.0.1`\n- UFW **inactive**\n- `sshd` listening on `0.0.0.0:22`\n\nIf all those are true, the host itself is fine.  \nIf ping/ssh fail **only inbound**, the block is almost certainly upstream (router or switch).\n\n---\n\n## \ud83e\udde9 Step 2 \u2013 Check layer 2 and layer 3 path from the MacBook\n\nFrom your MacBook:\n```bash\nping 10.0.0.110\narp -a | grep 10.0.0.110\n```\n\n- If `arp -a` **doesn\u2019t show a MAC address**, your switch or VLAN is isolating that port.  \n- If it *does* show a MAC address but ping still fails, the router or firewall is filtering ICMP/SSH traffic.\n\nSince the Ubuntu box *can* ping the MacBook, that confirms both are in the same subnet, so it\u2019s not a subnet mask issue \u2014 it\u2019s **one-way filtering**.\n\n### Fix on the router / switch:\n- Make sure the port that the Ubuntu box is on is **untagged in the LAN VLAN** (no isolation).\n- Disable any \u201cport isolation\u201d or \u201cAP isolation\u201d features.\n- Allow inbound TCP 22 (SSH) and ICMP echo on that VLAN.\n\n---\n\n## \ud83e\udde9 Step 3 \u2013 Persist DHCP on boot\n\nOnce connectivity is verified, lock in your DHCP config so the same IP comes back:\n\nEdit `/etc/netplan/01-dhcp.yaml`:\n```yaml\nnetwork:\n  version: 2\n  renderer: networkd\n  ethernets:\n    enp3s0:\n      dhcp4: true\n```\n\nApply and test:\n```bash\nsudo netplan apply\n```\n\nReboot and check:\n```bash\nip addr show enp3s0\n```\nIf it still picks up a DHCP address (maybe `.110` again), persistence works.\n\n---\n\n### \u2705 Quick verification matrix\n\n| Test | Command | Expected |\n|------|----------|-----------|\n| Outbound ping | `ping 8.8.8.8` | Works |\n| DNS | `dig google.com` | Resolves |\n| Inbound ping | `ping 10.0.0.110` from Mac | Works |\n| SSH inbound | `ssh user@10.0.0.110` | Login prompt |\n\n---\n\nOnce inbound ping + SSH work, you can safely:\n- Power off the display and keyboard.  \n- Start loading your 10 drives.  \n\nWould you like me to include a small **connectivity-test script** you can re-run after each reboot, so you don\u2019t have to manually type these each time?"
