ble   0x0008   100   100   000    Old_age   Offline      -       0\n199 UDMA_CRC_Error_Count    0x000a   200   200   000    Old_age   Always       -       1131\nclexp@bub03:~$ `\n\nI take issue with these results.  ther are all 1131 errors.  this is super unlikely given my randmon amount of random wiggling.  I think I will get this on the 'good' port.  I will try it next, and on the asmedia. I also do not think repeatde 1131 is a power or signal cable issue.  unless it continues to trial until it makes 1131 failed attempts then moves on (odd number though, I would expect a round number like 100, or 500 or 1000)\n\nhmm put the boot disck on the eSATA, but did not seem to boot, moved the boot to a 'faulty' sata port.  \n\nwith the boot drive in port 3, it won't boot.  so booting only on sata port1.  port 2 and 3 no good\n===\nboot drive back on port 1, 'known good' drive on eSATA.  nothing coming up on the head on the piKVM.  is the eSATA preventing boot? the eSATA 'should' be good for hot plug, but it is clearly on the same bus as the internal SATA ports.  pi kvm power is on the led, the network port is green and yellow, the csi brigde has the red led on, I think it is ok, and the web page is fine too.  let see if we can boot just one drive\n===\njust the boot ssd on the port one now.  nothing coming up on the screen.  not even bios.  \n===\nmachine direct to monitor, boot disc only in port4.  no bios.  did we kill this mainboard?\n===\nssd only in port5, nil on boot. power on but nothig to screen, without asmedia card\n\nin all cases waiting for ages and ssh just locks.  cann't even ping.  \n\nconclusion: \n1. this is now a dead board. \n2. if it pop back to life on another boot, this is too unstable to use.  It is now out and the multi disc array option is no more.  \n\nquestions:\n1. did it blow the discs?\n2. did it blow the PSU?\n3. can we power check the psu, with a volt meter?\n4. can we sell the ram? 4 * 1GB sticks?\n5. the case is good.  \n\nwhere do we go n