              "This is a great time to pause and size things properly, because rack **depth and width** are the biggest gotchas when moving from \u201cPC gear on shelves\u201d to \u201crack gear\u201d.  \n\n---\n\n## \ud83d\udccf Rack Standards (the basics)\n- **Width:**  \n  - Standard rack width is **19 inches (482.6 mm)** between mounting rails.  \n  - All \u201crackmount\u201d cases you see (1U\u20134U) are built to fit this.  \n  - Consumer gear (router, APC UPS, small switches) may not be rackmountable unless you buy ears/brackets or sit them on a shelf.  \n\n- **Height:**  \n  - \u201c1U\u201d = 1.75 inches (44.45 mm).  \n  - A 4U case = 7 inches tall.  \n  - You add up all your devices (UPS, switches, servers) to decide total U.  \n\n- **Depth:**  \n  - This is where people trip up.  \n  - Shallow telecom racks are ~450\u2013600 mm deep.  \n  - Data-center racks are 800\u20131000 mm deep (too big for a study).  \n  - Many hobbyist cases (like the Codegen 4U, at 500 mm) fit fine in a 600 mm deep rack.  \n  - Enterprise servers (Dell/HP/Supermicro) can be 700\u2013800 mm+ deep, and won\u2019t fit in a shallow rack.  \n\n---\n\n## \ud83d\uddc4\ufe0f Your Planned Setup\n- **APC Back-UPS 700:** not rackmount (sit on a shelf). Depth ~336 mm.  \n- **Router (Odyssey J4105 or similar):** not rackmount, shelf. Small depth.  \n- **TP-Link SG3428:** rack ears available, only ~230 mm deep.  \n- **Main server (Codegen 4U, 500 mm deep):** this is the biggest item. Needs at least a 600 mm deep rack.  \n- **Web server (another small ATX/mATX case, maybe 4U):** assume 400\u2013500 mm deep.  \n\n**Total U height estimate:**  \n- UPS shelf ~2U  \n- Router shelf ~1U  \n- Switch ~1U  \n- Main server (4U)  \n- Web server (3\u20134U)  \n- Allow spare 1\u20132U for airflow/future  \n\n\ud83d\udc49 ~12U total feels right.  \n\n---\n\n## \ud83d\udce6 So, What Rack Do You Need?\n- **Width:** standard 19\u2033 (482.6 mm). Don\u2019t worry, that\u2019s the default.  \n- **Depth:** at least **600 mm usable internal depth**. This will take your Codegen 4U case (500 mm) plus cables comfortably.  \n- **Height:** 12\u201315U (to leave headroom).  \n- **Type:** a **floor-standing 12U 600 mm deep rack/cabinet** is ideal for a study. Wall-mount racks usually max out at 9\u201312U and may not take the weight of a full server + UPS.  \n\n---\n\n## \ud83d\udda5\ufe0f About the Case You Spotted (Codegen 4U, 500 mm deep)\n- It\u2019s actually a great choice for your build.  \n- It will **fit perfectly** in a 600 mm deep rack (with a few cm clearance for cables).  \n- If you tried to put it in a 450 mm deep telecom rack, it would **stick out the back** or not fit at all.  \n\n---\n\n## \u2705 Recommendation\n- **Buy the Codegen 4U 500 mm case** for your 6-disk ZFS server.  \n- **Choose a 12U floor-standing rack**, at least **600 mm deep**.  \n- Put UPS + router on a shelf, switch in its 1U, servers in 4U slots.  \n- This leaves you with a neat, professional-ish stack, with a little room to grow.  \n\n---\n\n\ud83d\udc49 Do you want me to do a quick scan of UK racks (12U, 600 mm depth, floor-standing) on eBay/Amazon so you can see concrete options that would fit this case?"
            ]
