              "Nice find \u2014 \u00a384 is a very good price for the **MSI PRO B760M-P DDR4**. Let\u2019s unpack the \u201cDDR4 Memory Boost 4800+MHz/OC\u201d part, because it looks more mysterious than it is.  \n\n---\n\n## 1. What It Means\n- **\u201cDDR4 Memory Boost 4800+MHz/OC\u201d** is MSI\u2019s way of saying:  \n  - The official Intel 12th/13th gen memory spec for DDR4 is **3200 MHz** (JEDEC standard).  \n  - The board supports **faster DDR4 speeds** (up to ~4800 MHz) if you enable **XMP profiles** in BIOS (that\u2019s the \u201cOC\u201d part = overclock).  \n  - \u201cMemory Boost\u201d is just MSI\u2019s marketing term for decent trace layout / BIOS profiles.  \n\n---\n\n## 2. How It Affects Your RAM Purchase\n- You can install **any DDR4 kit** (2133 \u2192 4800 MHz).  \n- If you buy 3200 MHz RAM, it will \u201cjust work\u201d at 3200 MHz.  \n- If you buy faster RAM (3600, 4000, 4400\u2026), the board can run it at those speeds *if you enable XMP*.  \n- For a **home server**, you don\u2019t need to chase high DDR4 speeds \u2014 **3200\u20133600 MHz** is the price/performance sweet spot.  \n\n---\n\n## 3. How It Affects Performance\n- **ZFS and VMs** care more about memory *capacity* and *stability* than raw MHz.  \n- Real-world difference between DDR4-3200 CL16 and DDR4-4000 CL18 is usually <5%.  \n- Disk I/O, network, and CPU (QuickSync) are your real bottlenecks \u2014 not RAM speed.  \n\n---\n\n## \u2705 Practical Advice\n- Buy **32 GB (2 \u00d7 16 GB) DDR4-3200 or DDR4-3600** from Crucial, Corsair, or Kingston.  \n- Don\u2019t overpay for 4000+ MHz DDR4 \u2014 you won\u2019t notice it in this workload.  \n- Stick to **two sticks** (dual channel) instead of one 32 GB stick. It doubles memory bandwidth, which ZFS metadata lookups will like.  \n\n---\n\n\ud83d\udc49 So the \u201c4800+ MHz/OC\u201d line is basically *telling gamers they can run fast RAM if they want*. For you, it just means \u201cyou can drop in affordable DDR4-3200/3600 and it\u2019ll be fine.\u201d  \n\n---\n\nDo you want me to suggest a couple of **concrete DDR4 kits (32 GB, good value in UK right now)** that will pair safely with this board?"
            ]
